    <section class="py-16 bg-white">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-5 lg:px-8">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-ink mb-8">How do we work?</h2>
        <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
          <div class="bg-warm rounded-2xl p-6 border border-warm-tertiary">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-2">Initial Assessment</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">In the first session we listen to you and your reason for coming. This session carries no commitment; simply share what you feel ready to.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-warm rounded-2xl p-6 border border-warm-tertiary">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-2">How We'll Go On</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">CBT, psychodynamic therapy, or the two used together. Which way we go on is something we talk through.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-warm rounded-2xl p-6 border border-warm-tertiary">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-2">Regular Sessions</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">We typically progress with 45-minute sessions once a week. Each session builds on the last.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-warm rounded-2xl p-6 border border-warm-tertiary">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink text-sm mb-2">Flexible Format</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">In-person at our Famagusta office or online sessions via secure video platform are both available.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-16 bg-warm">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-5 lg:px-8">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-ink mb-6">When do people come to individual therapy?</h2>
        <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">A problem does not need to be "big enough". Feeling overwhelmed, low or stuck is reason enough. If something has lasted longer than a couple of weeks, or has started to affect how your days work, that is a reasonable point to talk to someone.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">You do not need to wait for a crisis. Most people come while life is still running, but one part of it keeps catching.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-16 bg-white">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-5 lg:px-8">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-ink mb-6">What happens in a session?</h2>
        <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">A session lasts 45 minutes. You open the conversation; the psychologist listens, asks questions and shares what they notice. The next session picks up where the last one left off.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">You do not have to say everything. You decide what to share and when. Some subjects only become speakable months in, and that is ordinary.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Sessions and your personal information are protected in line with confidentiality principles.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

